{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1020859-adding-vtm-with-the-spear-and-crone","id":1020859,"title":"adding VtM with the Spear and Crone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-22T07:03:21-08:00","id":1020859,"title":"adding VtM with the Spear and Crone","content":"Would adding the story of Cain to the Spear and the story of Lilith to the Crone change their basic make up? I'm thinking they only add to it. Would they be &quot;branches&quot; of these covenants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:22:43-08:00","id":1020890,"title":"","content":"Branches they would be. As a default, those stories don't harm those Covenants at all, but variety is also a factor on a greater scope. It is unlikely for the Lancea et Sanctum to have a monolithic view on their own religion, as the very Roman Church they mimic don't have. And is on purpose of letting it open that the writers made the Testament of Longinus not go in the matters of vampire origins or the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> You can retcon it, though, in the Spear without too much trouble if you do prefer.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone is, by design, a collaboration between pagan religions with the Crone as a central theme. So, though it can have a more unified religion in a given domain, to the point of hunting &quot;heresy&quot; locally, on a larger scope it is intended to be more of a coalition of pagans to defend against the Spear's agenda, than a unified religion. So, by doing such in more than a local fashion, you're pretty much changing what the Circle represents in the setting.<br /> <br /> In other words, to the Circle it is feasible, but deviates considerably more from intended setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:41:06-08:00","id":1020900,"title":"","content":"Yes, they definitely would. The Lancea et Sanctum believe that Longinus was<br /> a.) Directly turned into a vampire by God, not Embraced by another vampire.<br /> b.) The first vampire to know and accept his role in God's plan.<br /> <br /> If every vampire is (believed to be) a descendant of Caine, Longinus' spontaneous Embrace doesn't make sense. And if the biblical Caine was cursed by God as punishment for the first murder, it seems strange for him not to have known his purpose. Besides, the Sanctified belief that vampires are chosen to be the monsters that frighten humanity into His good graces, Caine's punishment makes les sense.<br /> <br /> That's not to say the Caine myth can't be a thing that some vampires believe in Requiem. It's just that it wouldn't work as a Lancea et Sanctum belief. The Sanctified would probably consider it heresy. In fact, in Requiem for Rome there was mention of &quot;The Cainite Heresy&quot;, a group of vampires who did believe Cain was the first vampires. They were thought to have been wiped out by modern nights, but there is a Compact of human vampire hunters in Hunter the Vigil (specifically in Night Stalkers if I recall correctly) called The Cainite Conspiracy. They use vials of blood sent to them by mysterious benefactors who seem to know a lot about vampires in rituals taught to them by the same to perform blood magic against their vampire targets.<br /> <br /> I don't know too much about the Lilith story from Masquerade, but if it validates Christian beliefs, I doubt many Acolytes would be likely to put faith in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:47:05-08:00","id":1020902,"title":"","content":"Were not pointing to 'Cain Heresy' in <b>Lancea Sanctum</b> Covenant book? I would sware there was something of splinter group in Covenant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:55:28-08:00","id":1020904,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone! I've said it before that the Spear concept eludes me a bit. I believe I have a hold on the others or at least an idea how I want to do them. Thanks Charlaquin for pointing out the idea that Longinus is the first to know and accept his role in god's plan. That clears up a lot and I seemed to have over looked that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:04:40-08:00","id":1020910,"title":"","content":"Lilith is already part of the Circle of the Crone, with cults dedicated to her. Especially the Daeva. They draw upon far more mythologies than just the Alphabet of Ben Sira, however. Babylonian myth is quite popular in this case, as the Western Deava claim that region to be their place of origin. Other, non-western vamps point to other gods and figures.<br /> <br /> As for Caine? In Requiem for Rome / Fall of the Camarilla, the Cainite Heresy actually started off as an offshoot of the Lancea Et Sanctum that eventually evolved into a heresy, then spun off into a full Hunter Conspiracy. Even ignoring that, if you added in Caine as some &quot;first vampire&quot; myth that the LeS believed in, at no point will it be a major thing. The Lance follow Longinus, who's kind of a Jesus / Moses / Muhammad figure. It was Longinus who brought the Law and Purpose to vampire-kind. Its His teachings they follow. Any mythological &quot;first vampire&quot; would be nothing more than an interesting historical note for academics to squabble over in their free time.<br /> <br /> The major problem with trying to bring Masquerade's story into Requiem is that the former is pretty much all about Christian Creationism, and the latter is more cosmopolitian and open ended in its makeup. There are several kinds of &quot;angels&quot; and at least three variations of God in existance that I'm aware of, none of which are omnipotent beings that created the Earth. Several covenants believe in spontaneous Embraces, or theorize that vampires are actually different phenomenon that eventually converged into the Kindred we know tonight. The myth of Caine would just be one of many mythologies bouncing around, and given little though due to its irrelevance to society tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T14:29:47-08:00","id":1021009,"title":"","content":"Lilith's mythology draws from many sources, but I do find it interesting in its relation with the Abrahamic faith, precisely because it brings the core concept of the Mystery of the Crone and the Goddess to an otherwise patriarcal belief system. In Masquerade, it is a sweet subversion of the Patriarch, showing Adam, God, Satan and Caine each as childish violators with an obsession for control to compensate emotional immaturity, and Lilith surviving to learn through pain the lessons those men refused to teach her. Eventually she becomes the teacher, and is reviled for her power to eventually overcome them through hard-learned power and understanding of the world.<br /> <br /> The Spear have Longinus precisely as a Jesus figure. The Testament presents him as the perfect opposition to Jesus, a monster in every sense Jesus was a saint, perverted until the moment of revelation. Then the blood of the Savior touches him, and he Understand. Through this understanding, though, Longinus chooses damnation knowing what purpose God have for him. He becomes a dark preach, at the same time anti-Jesus, anti-Pope, but just another faithful servant of God. Here to teach the masses and lead to a kind of salvation where your bless relies in knowing you're doing a Divine Job through Damnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T07:23:52-08:00","id":1021269,"title":"","content":"I would argue Monachus is more anti-pope, codifying and giving structure to the teachings of a wandering preacher, the anti-Jesus. But yes, the Cainite heresy is equivalent to a Jew, Christian or Muslim saying that Moses, Jesus or Muhammad are great and all that, but Adam is the real deal, and everything after him was really kinda useless.<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with VtM stuff, but I haven't actually ever heard any actual beliefs beyond &quot;Caine was punished and turned into a vampire for the first murder&quot;. What do Cainites believe? How do they pray? What are their commandments? I've always liked Cainism as a good Judeo-centric equivalent of the Sanctum for Israeli Kindred, would be nice to take the opportunity to hash out what that actually means","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T07:57:47-08:00","id":1021275,"title":"","content":"In the VtM it usually sums up to &quot;Caine was the first&quot;. From this comes the Book of Nod, allegedly a transcription of the wanderings of Caine since its curse through the &quot;land of Nod&quot;. His encounter with the angels, each cursing and blessing in turn, his lone wanderings, the encounter with the Crone, and a lot more. Comes the First City, where Caine tried to see if God had forgiven him, and his conclusion after the Deluge that, well, clearly not. The siring of the Second and the Third Generations in the First City. Generation is kind of a BIG deal in VtM.<br /> <br /> Mostly it sums up to an epic journey, establishing a mythical frame for Kindred existence. It ends with the prophecies for the time of Gehenna, an element that colors much in Kindred society. It isn't quite a religion, though it did spawned some, like the Path of Caine and the Path of Lillith. Or the weird take of the Sabbat in Christian Roman Catholicism. But mostly, what the Cainite belief is is an origin myth that is explored in search for the origin of the curse, its possibilities, the dangers of the past and the doom lurking in the near future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T08:10:53-08:00","id":1021279,"title":"","content":"Yeah, unlike Longinism, Nodism doesn't have much dogma to speak of. It's an origin myth for vampires more than a religious denomination. Not that there aren't religious groups based on it, but at its core it's a story more than it is an ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:15:22-08:00","id":1021641,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember is that the Circle is not one religion, but an alliance of a great many bloody pagan cults. The Circle in your city could just as much believe in Lillith as they could believe in the Crone or Sekhmet or whoever else - or possibky all of the above, constantly fighting amongst themselves!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:51:13-08:00","id":1021652,"title":"","content":"It just occurred to me that, given how those covenants work, you could have, instead of Lancea and Circle in a city, two factions of the Circle fighting for power in the absence of a strong Spear enclave.<br /> <br /> And voila, those two could very well be Cainites and Lillin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}